COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[566,"§Al-Qalam, Al-Haqqah\ndeeds\nMaintain with care all daily prayers on time and in congregation.\nAdvise a Muslim who is persistent in sin, and do not despair.\nAsk Allah for a good end to your life.\nguid\nReminding of the Last Day.\nDo not hasten to see the results of your preaching to Allah.\nBe aware of the plights of past nations.\nrefl\nخَٰشِعَةً أَبۡصَٰرُهُمۡ تَرۡهَقُهُمۡ ذِلَّةٞۖ وَقَدۡ كَانُواْ يُدۡعَوۡنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ وَهُمۡ سَٰلِمُونَ ٤٣\nAttributing humbleness, which is submissiveness and humiliation, to the eyes because its effect will be visible in them. Al-Shawkani: 5/275.\nIn this verse, humbleness is attributed to the eyes. Why?\nوَقَدۡ كَانُواْ يُدۡعَوۡنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ وَهُمۡ سَٰلِمُونَ ٤٣\nIbrahim Al-Taymi said: They used to be called to obligatory prayers through the calls to prayer and Iqamah. Saeed bin Jubair said: They used to hear: \"Come to Success,\" but did not respond. Al-Baghawi: 4/454.\nWhat is meant by (And they used to be invited to prostration while they were sound)?\nفَذَرۡنِي وَمَن يُكَذِّبُ بِهَٰذَا ٱلۡحَدِيثِۖ سَنَسۡتَدۡرِجُهُم مِّنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٤\nMeaning: We will bring them to punishment step by step by giving them respite, keeping them healthy, and increasing our blessings upon them in ways that they do not perceive that will lead them to their doom. Rather, they claim they are being favored over the believers, even though it will lead to their ruin. Al-Alusi: 15/41.\nWhat is the sign of Allah's allurement to the deniers?\nسَنَسۡتَدۡرِجُهُم مِّنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٤\nSufyan Al-Thawri said: We increase our blessings upon them and make them forget to be grateful. Alhasan said: How many persons are led to their ruin by blessings, how many smitten persons by compliments, and how many deluded persons because they are shielded from people's eyes. Abu Roq said: Every time they sin, We renew a blessing for them, and make them forget to seek forgiveness. In a Prophetic Hadith: A man from the Children of Israel said: \"O Lord, how much I disobey You but do not punish me!\" So, Allah revealed to the Prophet of their times saying: Say to him: \"How much I punish you while you do not perceive; the dryness of your eyes and hardness of the heart are allurement and punishment from me if you only understand.\" Al-Qurtubi: 21/180.\nWhat is meant by the gradual leading mentioned in this verse?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ لِحُكۡمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ ٱلۡحُوتِ إِذۡ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكۡظُومٞ ٤٨\nHe was Jonah (u), and is called the Man of the Whale because the whale swallowed him. His story is mentioned in Surat Al-Anbiya and Surat As-Saffat. The Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) was forbidden from emulating him in wearisome and hastiness when he went off in anger. Ibn Juzay: 2/494.\nThe Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) was forbidden from emulating something. What is it?\nوَإِن يَكَادُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَيُزۡلِقُونَكَ بِأَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡ لَمَّا سَمِعُواْ ٱلذِّكۡرَ وَيَقُولُونَ إِنَّهُۥ لَمَجۡنُونٞ ٥١\nMeaning: If it was not for Allah's protection of you, they would have harmed you by gazing at you with their envious eyes due to their hatred of you. This verse proves that the effect of the evil eye is real by the command of Allah. Ibn Kathir: 4/408.\nIt is inferred from this verse that evil eye may cause harm. Explain.\nوَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكۡرٞ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٥٢\nMeaning: This Quran or this Messenger (ﷺ) (is not except a reminder), an admonishment and honor to (the worlds), all of them; the highly intelligent among them and the ordinary know that there is nothing like the Quran in its excellent meanings, beautiful wordings, great composition, fine insight, and ample formats. Everyone understands the Quran at the level that is made easy for him by Allah. Al-Biqai: 20/336.\nWhy do we not become bored when we recite the Holy Quran?\nwords\nتَرهَقُهُمThey will be Covered\nمَكظُومٌDistressed\nلَنُبِذَ بِالعَرَاءِHe would have been thrown onto the barren shore\nوَهُوَ مَذمُومٌHe was blameworthy\nلَيُزلِقُونَكَThey would make you fall down with their malicious gazes\nعَاتِيَةٍViolent wind\nحُسُومًاIn succession\nأَعجَازُ نَخلٍTrunks of palm trees"],[567,"§Al-Haqqah\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to have your Record in your right hand on the Day of Resurrection.\nGive to a charity.\nFeed a needy person.\nguid\nAbandon hidden sins, as no secret is hidden from Allah.\nRemind yourself of the immense terrors of the Day of Resurrection.\nThe servant's wealth and authority will not avail him anything when Allah's punishment strikes him.\nrefl\nوَتَعِيَهَآ أُذُنٞ وَٰعِيَةٞ ١٢\nAttentiveness can be attributed to the ears as well as the heart. They say: An attentive heart and attentive ears. The ears and hearts are linked, as knowledge is heard by the ears and goes to the heart. Hence, the ears are the gate, the messenger, and the deliverer of knowledge to the heart while the tongue is a messenger of the heart, which conveys what is in it. Whoever knew the links between physical limbs and the heart, would realize that the ears are more deserving to be described as (attentive), and that when they take heed, the heart does too. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/189.\nThe ears are described as (attentive). Why?\nلِنَجۡعَلَهَا لَكُمۡ تَذۡكِرَةٗ وَتَعِيَهَآ أُذُنٞ وَٰعِيَةٞ ١٢\nTaking heed: Grasping what is being said by having attentive ears that are heedful. This alludes to the polytheists who were not admonished by the news of the Deluge and the Ark by which the believers were saved, so they took this news heedlessly. Ibn Ashur: 29/123.\nThis verse alludes to the polytheists. Explain.\nإِنِّي ظَنَنتُ أَنِّي مُلَٰقٍ حِسَابِيَهۡ ٢٠\nThe more virtuous a person is, the more he feels his shortcomings. The fear of Allah which induces doing good deeds is sufficient for a prudent person. Al-Biqai: 20/362.\nWhat is the sign of a man's prudence?\nكُلُواْ وَٱشۡرَبُواْ هَنِيٓـَٔۢا بِمَآ أَسۡلَفۡتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَيَّامِ ٱلۡخَالِيَةِ ٢٤\nIt is narrated in authentic Hadith that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"None amongst you can get into Paradise by virtue of his deeds alone. They said: Allah's Messenger, not even you? He said: Not even I, but that Allah should wrap me in His Grace and Mercy.\" Ibn Taimyah: 6/388.\nWhen do good deeds benefit the servant?\nثُمَّ فِي سِلۡسِلَةٖ ذَرۡعُهَا سَبۡعُونَ ذِرَاعٗا فَٱسۡلُكُوهُ ٣٢ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ٣٣ وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلۡمِسۡكِينِ ٣٤\nAbu-Darda' (t) used to encourage his wife to cook more of the stew to feed the needy, and say: We removed one-half of the chain with faith, should we not remove the other half? Referring to this verse. Al-Alusi: 15/57.\nWhat are the rewards for faith and charity to the needy when performed by the believer?\nوَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلۡمِسۡكِينِ ٣٤\nDescribing him as: (Nor did he encourage feeding the needy) indicates that he did not feed him in the first place. This verse indicates the great virtue of charity since Allah links the prevention of feeding the needy to disbelief in Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/494.\nThis verse indicates the great virtue of charity. How?\nإِنَّهُۥ كَانَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ٣٣ وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلۡمِسۡكِينِ ٣٤\nThat is because the foundation and essence of attaining happiness are two things: Sincerity toward Allah, which is rooted in faith in Allah, and kindness toward people, which takes many forms, one of the greatest of which is meeting the needs of the needy by feeding them what they need for nourishment. But these people have no sincerity and show no kindness, so they deserve that punishment. Al-Saadi: 884.\nThe doomed people are described as not believing in Allah, the Most Great, and they do encourage feeding the needy. Why?\nwords\nوَالمُؤتَفِكَاتُThe overturned cities, people of Lot (u)\nبِالخَاطِئَةِWith the grave sins\nرَابِيَةًA severe punishment\nوَاهِيَةٌWeak, frail\nهَاؤُمُHere it is\nفَغُلُّوهُShackle him\nصَلُّوهُThrow him in Hell to burn\nذَرعُهَاIts length in angels' cubit"],[568,"§Al-Haqqah, Al-Ma'arij\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from uttering a lie, or committing a wicked act.\"\nSay, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He, Glorified is Allah the Great,\" a hundred times.\nSay, \"O Allah, guide me to the best qualities, as You alone can guide me to the best of them.\"\nguid\nIf the Prophet (ﷺ) was warned against attributing something to Allah, how about one who gives fatwa without knowledge and attributes it to Allah?\nFalse prophets have the worst end to their lives.\nSure faith about the Last Day and its nearness encourages the faithful to do good deeds.\nrefl\nتَنزِيلٞ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٤٣\n(It is a revelation from the Lord of the worlds), this implies that His complete Lordship over His creation, [man and jinn], will not ever leave them neglected; where He does not command, nor forbid, nor guide them to what benefits them, or warn them against what may harm them, and leave them like grazing livestock. Whoever claims that, does not revere Allah His true reverence, and attributes to Him that which is not suitable for Him. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/191.\nWhat is the sign of Allah's complete Lordship?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَتَذۡكِرَةٞ لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٤٨\nMeaning: A reminder for the righteous from among the worlds, as they are the ones who benefit from the Quran because they turn to it seeking its benefits. Al-Biqai: 20/383.\nThe righteous are singled out for reminder. Why?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ صَبۡرٗا جَمِيلًا ٥\n(So be patient), endure their annoyance patiently, and that should not stop you from conveying the Message to them. You have come close to the time of taking retribution from them. O the victor, the last of the Prophets to whom I have revealed that which I have not revealed to anyone else. Patience is holding oneself against what is dislikable. Al-Biqai: 20/392.\nDoes bearing patiently with people entail neglecting to preach them? Explain.\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ صَبۡرٗا جَمِيلًا ٥\nIt means patience without discontent. Al-Tabari: 23/603.\nWhat is the meaning of gracious patience?\nإِنَّهُمۡ يَرَوۡنَهُۥ بَعِيدٗا ٦ وَنَرَىٰهُ قَرِيبٗا ٧\nBut Allah sees it as being close at hand because He is Kind and Forbearing and does not hasten. He knows that it will inevitably come to pass, and every awaited event is near. Al-Saadi: 886.\n1,400 years had passed since the revelation of this verse, but the Day of Resurrection is described as (near). How?\nيَوۡمَ تَكُونُ ٱلسَّمَآءُ كَٱلۡمُهۡلِ ٨ وَتَكُونُ ٱلۡجِبَالُ كَٱلۡعِهۡنِ ٩\nIf all these troubles will happen to these massive entities (the mountains), what do you think will happen to a weak human being, whose back is laden with sins and heavy burdens? Al-Saadi: 886\nWhat is the lesson learned from mentioning the changes to the heavens and mountains? How?\nوَتَكُونُ ٱلۡجِبَالُ كَٱلۡعِهۡنِ ٩\nThe mountains are likened to the wool when it puffs up and becomes disjointed. Ibn Juzay: 2/495.\nThere is a similarity between wool and mountains on the Day of Resurrection. Explain.\nwords\nغِسلِينٍThe discharge of wounds\nتَقَوَّلَHe had falsely attributed\nالوَتِينَThe aorta, life artery of the heart\nذِي المَعَارِجِThe Lord of the ways of ascent\nكَالمُهلِLike murky oil\nكَالعِهنِLike dyed wool"],[569,"§Al-Ma'arij\ndeeds\nMaintain with care all daily prayers in congregation at the mosque.\nGive to a charity.\nRecall a trust or a pledge that you had made to someone and fulfill it.\nguid\nPerforming prayers in humbleness protects one from anxiety and despair.\nKeep your promises and fulfill your pledges.\nGuard yourself against prohibited desires.\nrefl\nيُبَصَّرُونَهُمۡۚ يَوَدُّ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُ لَوۡ يَفۡتَدِي مِنۡ عَذَابِ يَوۡمِئِذِۢ بِبَنِيهِ ١١ وَصَٰحِبَتِهِۦ وَأَخِيهِ ١٢ وَفَصِيلَتِهِ ٱلَّتِي تُـٔۡوِيهِ ١٣ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗا ثُمَّ يُنجِيهِ ١٤\nAllah, the Almighty, begins by mentioning the children, the wife, and the brother, to inform His servants of the great calamities in which the disbeliever will be on the Day of Resurrection that he wishes to ransom himself with the most beloved and closest people to him. Al-Tabari: 23/606.\nAllah mentions man's relatives in a certain order. Why?\n۞إِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ خُلِقَ هَلُوعًا ١٩ إِذَا مَسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ جَزُوعٗا ٢٠ وَإِذَا مَسَّهُ ٱلۡخَيۡرُ مَنُوعًا ٢١ إِلَّا ٱلۡمُصَلِّينَ ٢٢\nA human soul is inherently a pursuer and a striver, and when is not directed toward a righteous cause, it will pursue an evil one and engage in bad deeds. Allah says, (Indeed, mankind was created impatient ` When evil befalls him, he bewails ` And when good fortune comes his way, he becomes tight-fisted ` Except those who pray). Allah says that man is created as such, and whoever acts differently, is because of Allah's favor and bounty. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/196.\nWhen you know that every person has a will, what should be your duty?\n۞إِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ خُلِقَ هَلُوعًا ١٩ إِذَا مَسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ جَزُوعٗا ٢٠ وَإِذَا مَسَّهُ ٱلۡخَيۡرُ مَنُوعًا ٢١ إِلَّا ٱلۡمُصَلِّينَ ٢٢\nAllah mentions these human characteristics as a rebuke to those who have them, and that is why He makes an exception for those who pray because their prayers induce them to have little regard for worldly life, so they do not bewail its evil, nor withhold its fortune. Ibn Juzay: 2/49.\nAllah makes an exception for those who pray from being impatient. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هُم مِّنۡ عَذَابِ رَبِّهِم مُّشۡفِقُونَ ٢٧\nMeaning: They are fearful for themselves despite having done good deeds, however, they belittle their deeds and hold the position of Allah in the highest regard, as Allah says, (And they who give what they give while their hearts are fearful because they will be returning to their Lord)[23:60]. Al-Alusi: 15/71.\nWhen the servant is more fearful of Allah, his righteous deeds increase. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هُم بِشَهَٰدَٰتِهِمۡ قَآئِمُونَ ٣٣\nAllah alone is worshiped through all types of worships, which is a manifestation of the testimony to the Oneness of Allah. That is why He has forbidden the Fire punishment of one who testifies to His Oneness truthfully. It will not be possible for one who manifests true adherence to this testimony to enter the Fire, as Allah says, (And who are upright in their testimonies). Hence, he is upright in his testimony inwardly and outwardly, as some people have dead testimonies, while others are heedless but when alerted, they become heedful. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/197.\nHow is the manifestation of the testimony to the Oneness of Allah realized?\nٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَلَىٰ صَلَاتِهِمۡ دَآئِمُونَ ٢٣ وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَلَىٰ صَلَاتِهِمۡ يُحَافِظُونَ ٣٤\nThe mention of prayer is repeated because, in the first verse, Allah describes their constancy of prayer, where they are not distracted from it by anything else. In the second verse, Allah mentions their maintenance of prayer, where they observe all of its pillars, conditions, and sunnah. Al-Shawkani: 5/293.\nThe mention of prayer is repeated. Why?\nكَلَّآۖ إِنَّا خَلَقۡنَٰهُم مِّمَّا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٩\nThe meaning of this verse comprises three aspects, first: Showing the reality of man's origins as a response to those who are arrogant. Second: Responding to the disbelievers who wish to enter Paradise, as if saying: We created you from the same substance that all people have been created from, hence, all people are equal, and no one will enter Paradise except with righteous deeds. Third: A proof of resurrection; since Allah created them from a weak fluid, then He is certainly capable of resurrecting them, as He says, (Had he not been a sperm from semen emitted?)[75:37]. Ibn Juzay: 2/495.\nThe meaning of this verse comprises three aspects, What are they?\nwords\nوَفَصِيلَتِهِHis kindred\nلَظَىFlame of Hell\nنَزَّاعَةً لِلشَّوَىRemoves the skin of the head and body extremities\nفَأَوعَىHoarded his wealth\nهَلُوعًاImpatient\nجَزُوعًاHe bewails when evil befalls him"],[570,"§Al-Ma'arij, Nuh\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, and I seek protection in You from You. I cannot enumerate Your praises, You are as You have praised Yourself.\"\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the cessation of Your blessing, the change of Your protection (from me), Your sudden vengeance, and all of Your anger.\"\nPreach to Allah by sending a message, a voice or video recording, advising someone, or by any suitable means.\nguid\nAllah's capability has no match.\nThis is a reminder of the rushing out of the graves in humiliation.\nPatience is the cornerstone of every preacher's call.\nrefl\nفَذَرۡهُمۡ يَخُوضُواْ وَيَلۡعَبُواْ حَتَّىٰ يُلَٰقُواْ يَوۡمَهُمُ ٱلَّذِي يُوعَدُونَ ٤٢\nEngaging in falsehood is the opposite of speaking the truth, and amusement is the opposite of a beneficial endeavor. The former is the opposite of useful knowledge, and the latter is the opposite of righteous deeds. Hence, they did not speak the truth, nor did they do the right thing, and that is the way of those who turned away from what the Messenger brought - they have to do both of them. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/201\nWhat are the signs of those who turned away from the Messenger?\nخَٰشِعَةً أَبۡصَٰرُهُمۡ تَرۡهَقُهُمۡ ذِلَّةٞۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡيَوۡمُ ٱلَّذِي كَانُواْ يُوعَدُونَ ٤٤\nAfter the description that includes intense warning, this Surah concludes with: (That is the Day which they had been promised), which affirms that their question at the beginning of this Surah, (A questioner asked for a punishment bound to happen) was made only for mocking and casting doubt. Hence, Allah makes clear to them what they will face in the Hereafter so that they take heed and return to their Lord. This links the conclusion of this Surah to its beginning. Al-Shanqiti: 8/305.\nWhat is the link between the beginning and conclusion of this Surah?\nإِنَّآ أَرۡسَلۡنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦٓ أَنۡ أَنذِرۡ قَوۡمَكَ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن يَأۡتِيَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ١\nAllah does not say, \"Warn the people\", rather He says, (Warn your people) to encourage Noah (u) to strive for their salvation since his sons, relatives, and loved ones were among them. Ibn Ashur: 29/187.\nAllah does not say, \"Warn the people\", rather He says, (Warn your people). Why?\nقَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ إِنِّي لَكُمۡ نَذِيرٞ مُّبِينٌ ٢\nNoah (u) began inviting them by saying, (O my people) to attract their attention and make them more likely to accept what he was about to say, as he wished for them what he wished for himself. He emphasized his invitation to them by using, (indeed), as they were hesitant to believe him. Ibn Ashur: 29/188.\nNoah (u) began inviting them by saying, (O my people). Why?\nأَنِ ٱعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱتَّقُوهُ وَأَطِيعُونِ ٣\nHe made the worship and fear to Allah, and made the obedience to the Messenger, as whoever obeys the Messenger has indeed obeyed Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 6/398.\nNoah (u) commanded them to worship and fear Allah while obeying him. Why?\nوَإِنِّي كُلَّمَا دَعَوۡتُهُمۡ لِتَغۡفِرَ لَهُمۡ\nMeaning: I invited them to believe so that You would forgive them. Forgiveness, which is a result of faith, is mentioned to show their abhorrent evasion of him; where they evaded what would lead them to their happiness. Ibn Juzay: 2/494.\nAllah mentions forgiveness, but does not mention its cause, which is faith. Why?\nثُمَّ إِنِّي دَعَوۡتُهُمۡ جِهَارٗا ٨ ثُمَّ إِنِّيٓ أَعۡلَنتُ لَهُمۡ وَأَسۡرَرۡتُ لَهُمۡ إِسۡرَارٗا ٩\nNoah (u) mentioned first that he invited them by night and day, then, he called them openly, then he combined between calling them openly and privately. That was the ultimate effort in providing his advice and conveying the Message, (u). Ibn Juzay: 2/495.\nThe invitation by Noah (u) to his people was diverse. What does that indicate?\nwords\nبِمَسبُوقِينَNone can escape Our decree\nالأَجدَاثِThe Graves\nنُصُبٍIdols made of stone\nيُوفِضُونَRushing toward\nوَاستَغشَوا ثِيَابَهُمCovered themselves with their garments\nوَأَصَرُّواPersisted in disbelief"],[571,"§Nuh\ndeeds\nReflect on the creation of heavens and earth, then draw two useful lessons.\nSay, \"O Allah, we make You our shield against them, and take refuge with You from their evils.\"\nSay: [My Lord, forgive me and my parents, and whoever enters my house as a believer, and all the believing men and women, and do not increase the wrongdoers except in ruin]\nguid\nAsking often for Allah's forgiveness brings rain, shields against poverty, and cures Infertility.\nIn every society, there are callers to good and callers to evil.\nGlorifying Allah and venerating Him by not associating partners with Him is obligatory.\nrefl\nفَقُلۡتُ ٱسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ غَفَّارٗا ١٠ يُرۡسِلِ ٱلسَّمَآءَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّدۡرَارٗا ١١\nThis verse proves that asking for forgiveness is a cause for the coming of the rain. When Omar bin Al-Khattab (t) went out to pray for rain, he did not say more than asking for Allah's forgiveness and left, then it was said to him: You did not ask Allah for rain! He replied: By Allah, I have asked Him in the best and most eloquent way. Ibn Juzay: 2/495.\nAsking for Allah's forgiveness is important when praying for rain. Explain.\nمَّا لَكُمۡ لَا تَرۡجُونَ لِلَّهِ وَقَارٗا ١٣\nMeaning: Why do you not fear Allah's might and His power to punish any of you; there is no excuse for you not to be fearful of Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 21/255.\nWhat is meant by (you do not fear)?\nمَّا لَكُمۡ لَا تَرۡجُونَ لِلَّهِ وَقَارٗا ١٣\nHad they venerated Allah and recognized His greatness, they would have believed in His Oneness, obeyed and thanked Him, as obeying Him, avoiding His prohibitions, and being modest with Him are commensurate with the level of veneration of Him in the heart. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/203.\nWhat is the sign of the veneration of Allah in the heart?\nقَالَ نُوحٞ رَّبِّ إِنَّهُمۡ عَصَوۡنِي وَٱتَّبَعُواْ مَن لَّمۡ يَزِدۡهُ مَالُهُۥ وَوَلَدُهُۥٓ إِلَّا خَسَارٗا ٢١\nProsperity in this life was the reason for their tyranny, insolence, and following their desires until they disbelieved, exploited others, and overwhelmed them, hence they became the cause for their wretchedness and loss with their own loss. Al-Biqai: 20/447.\nExplain the bad omen of following the deviated wealthy and neglecting to follow the righteous.\nإِنَّكَ إِن تَذَرۡهُمۡ يُضِلُّواْ عِبَادَكَ وَلَا يَلِدُوٓاْ إِلَّا فَاجِرٗا كَفَّارٗا ٢٧\nMeaning: Their continued existence is absolutely detrimental to them and others. Noah (u) only said that because after mixing with them a great deal, and because of what he had experienced of their manners and attitude, he had reached that conclusion based on what he knew of their misdeeds. No wonder Allah responded to his prayer and drowned them all, but He saved Noah and the believers who were with him. Al-Saadi: 889.\nNoah (u) invoked Allah against his people. Why?\nرَّبِّ ٱغۡفِرۡ لِي وَلِوَٰلِدَيَّ وَلِمَن دَخَلَ بَيۡتِيَ مُؤۡمِنٗا وَلِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِۖ\nFrom this verse, it can be learned that when supplicating, it is a sunnah to begin with oneself before others. Ibn Juzay: 2/495.\nWhat can be learned from Noah's (u) supplication\nرَّبِّ ٱغۡفِرۡ لِي وَلِوَٰلِدَيَّ وَلِمَن دَخَلَ بَيۡتِيَ مُؤۡمِنٗا وَلِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِۖ\nThese people are singled out for mention to affirm their rights and give them priority when it comes to showing kindness. Then he made his supplication more general. Al-Saadi: 890.\nThe parents are singled out for mention before the believers. Why?\nwords\nمِدرَارًاContinuing rain showers\nأَطوَارًاIn stages\nفِجَاجًاSpacious paths\nلاَ تَذَرُنَّDo not abandon\nدَيَّارًاA single disbeliever on earth\nتَبَارًاRuin, loss"],[572,"§Al-Jinn\ndeeds\nRecite some verses of the Quran while sensing that the angels and jinn listen to your reciting so that you may be rewarded for that.\nWhen going to bed, say, \"O Allah, I submitted my soul to You, I have turned my face toward You, I entrusted my affair to You, and committed my back to You in hope and fear of You. There is no refuge or safe haven from You except with You. I believed in Your Book which You have revealed and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.\"\nIn the morning and evening, seek refuge in the Perfect Words of Allah from the evil of what He has created.\nguid\nBelieving in the existence of jinn is part of the believer's faith.\nVenerate Allah, the Almighty.\nShirk weakens the servant while believing in the Oneness of Allah increases his strength and honor.\nrefl\nيَهۡدِيٓ إِلَى ٱلرُّشۡدِ فَـَٔامَنَّا بِهِۦۖ وَلَن نُّشۡرِكَ بِرَبِّنَآ أَحَدٗا ٢\nThis is a rebuke to the disbelievers among mankind for not benefiting from the Quran while the jinn believed in it once they heard it for the first time, benefited from listening to a few verses, realized that this is the word of Allah, and believed in it. Al-Shawkani: 5/303-304.\nThe jinn believed when they heard the Quran for the first time. What lesson is drawn from that?\nوَأَنَّا ظَنَنَّآ أَن لَّن تَقُولَ ٱلۡإِنسُ وَٱلۡجِنُّ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبٗا ٥\nThis shows that one should not emulate others, as trusting everyone is naïve, and that is learned through experience. Emulation may lead to disbelief and eternal doom. An-Nu'man bin Bashir (t) reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"So he who guards against doubtful things keeps his religion and his honor blameless.\" This proves that one must not take up any religious fundamentals without a clear proof. Al-Biqai: 20/471.\nEmulation can be good and can be bad. Explain.\nوَأَنَّهُۥ كَانَ رِجَالٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡإِنسِ يَعُوذُونَ بِرِجَالٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡجِنِّ فَزَادُوهُمۡ رَهَقٗا ٦\nMeaning: When men sought refuge with the jinn, the jinn increased them in misguidance and sins, or increased their fear when they realized their ignorance. Moreover, it is said that when men sought refuge with the jinn, the jinn's arrogance and tyranny had increased until one among them said: I am the master of jinn and mankind. Ibn Juzay: 2/495.\nExplain the harm caused by some people who seek help from magicians and soothsayers.\nوَأَنَّا لَا نَدۡرِيٓ أَشَرٌّ أُرِيدَ بِمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ أَمۡ أَرَادَ بِهِمۡ رَبُّهُمۡ رَشَدٗا ١٠\nThe intent of evil is not attributed to Allah, rather, a passive voice is used to describe it. Unlike the intent of good, which is attributed to Him, as saying: (or their Lord intends good for them). This conforms to the etiquette of not attributing the intent of evil to Allah. Ibn Ashur: 29/231.\nEven though Allah decrees all things, the jinn did not attribute the evil intent to Him. Why?\nوَأَنَّا مِنَّا ٱلصَّٰلِحُونَ وَمِنَّا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَۖ كُنَّا طَرَآئِقَ قِدَدٗا ١١\nWhen the jinn began inviting their brethren to follow the path of good, they did not directly accuse them of corruption, rather, they said: (And among us are some who are righteous) then, gently, they said: (And some who are otherwise). Ibn Ashur: 29/232.\nWhat etiquette is learned by a preacher from this verse?\nوَأَنَّا لَمَّا سَمِعۡنَا ٱلۡهُدَىٰٓ ءَامَنَّا بِهِۦۖ فَمَن يُؤۡمِنۢ بِرَبِّهِۦ فَلَا يَخَافُ بَخۡسٗا وَلَا رَهَقٗا ١٣\nHe will not fear deprivation or burden because he did not deprive anyone of his right, nor did he wrong anyone, hence, he should not fear their requitals. Al-Alusi: 15/100.\nThe requital befits the action. Explain in light of this verse.\nفَمَن يُؤۡمِنۢ بِرَبِّهِۦ فَلَا يَخَافُ بَخۡسٗا وَلَا رَهَقٗا ١٣\nIbn Abbas (k) said: He will not fear reduction of his good deeds, nor will the evil of another be placed upon him, as deprivation is reduction, and burden is oppression. Al-Qurtubi: 21/292.\nIs it conceivable that the servant's good deeds will be reduced, and his evil deeds will increase?\nwords\nجَدُّ رَبِّنَاThe Majesty of our Lord\nسَفِيهُنَاIblees\nرَهَقًاTyranny\nمَقَاعِدَ لِلسَّمعِPositions for eavesdropping\nرَصَدًاLying in wait for him\nطَرَائِقَ قِدَدًاDifferent ways, groups"],[573,"§Al-Jinn\ndeeds\nSay, \"None is worthy of worship but Allah alone, Who has no partner. To Him belongs all sovereignty and all praise, and He is Capable over all things.\" ten times.\nSupplicate Allah at the mosque between the call to prayer (Athan) and Iqamah to fulfill one of your wishes for you.\nSupplicate Allah by saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nguid\nAll benefits and harms are in the Hand of Allah, so do not let your heart be attached to anyone else.\nAllah has exclusive knowledge of the unseen.\nAllah is the Great and His knowledge encompasses all things.\nrefl\nوَأَلَّوِ ٱسۡتَقَٰمُواْ عَلَى ٱلطَّرِيقَةِ لَأَسۡقَيۡنَٰهُم مَّآءً غَدَقٗا ١٦\nThe right way is Islam's way and obedience to Allah. This means that if people had remained straight on that, Allah would have bestowed abundant provisions on them. It is similar to this verse, (And if only the people of the cities had believed and feared Allah, We would have opened [bestowed] upon them blessings from the heaven and the earth)[7:96]. Ibn Juzay: 2/497.\nIn light of this verse, describe the end result for people in this life when they remain steadfast on the right way.\nوَأَلَّوِ ٱسۡتَقَٰمُواْ عَلَى ٱلطَّرِيقَةِ لَأَسۡقَيۡنَٰهُم مَّآءً غَدَقٗا ١٦\nOmar (t) said: \"Wherever there is water, there is wealth, and wherever there is wealth, there is a trial. Likening great provision to abundant water because all goodness and provisions are the result of rain, hence, it is expressed as such.\" Al-Qurtubi: 21/295.\nWhy is water mentioned in this verse?\nوَأَنَّ ٱلۡمَسَٰجِدَ لِلَّهِ فَلَا تَدۡعُواْ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ أَحَدٗا ١٨\nMeaning: Dedicate the mosques to Allah's remembrance, and do not make them places for your mockery, trading, sitting, or roadways. Do not share the mosques of Allah with anyone else. Al-Qurtubi: 21/300.\nMosques are dedicated by Allah for one thing only. What is it?\nقُلۡ إِنِّي لَآ أَمۡلِكُ لَكُمۡ ضَرّٗا وَلَا رَشَدٗا ٢١\nThis implies a great warning and entrusting all affairs to Allah that He, the Almighty, would recompense him for his righteous deeds and punish them for their evil deeds. Al-Alusi: 15/105.\nWhat are the implications of negating benefit and harm by the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nقُلۡ إِنِّي لَن يُجِيرَنِي مِنَ ٱللَّهِ أَحَدٞ وَلَنۡ أَجِدَ مِن دُونِهِۦ مُلۡتَحَدًا ٢٢\nMeaning: There is no one I would take as a refuge could rescue me from the punishment of Allah. If the Messenger (ﷺ), who is the most perfect of all people, has no power to cause harm or bring benefit, and cannot ward off from himself any ill that Allah may intend for him, then it is even more applicable to other humans. Al-Saadi: 891.\nThis verse indicates the misguidance of those whose hearts are attached to the righteous. Explain.\nعَٰلِمُ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ فَلَا يُظۡهِرُ عَلَىٰ غَيۡبِهِۦٓ أَحَدًا ٢٦ إِلَّا مَنِ ٱرۡتَضَىٰ مِن رَّسُولٖ\nHere, the messengers are from both: Angels and men. Ibn Kathir: 4/43.\nDoes revealing some of the unseen limited to human messengers? Do angels know the unseen?\nلِّيَعۡلَمَ أَن قَدۡ أَبۡلَغُواْ رِسَٰلَٰتِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَأَحَاطَ بِمَا لَدَيۡهِمۡ وَأَحۡصَىٰ كُلَّ شَيۡءٍ عَدَدَۢا ٢٨\nMeaning: Allah's knowledge of all things is not in a general way, rather, it is to the smallest details, which means that He knows each one of His creations in a specific way. Al-Shawkani: 5/313.\nIs Allah's knowledge general or is it detailed?\nwords\nوَأَلَّوِ استَقَامُواIf they had remained steadfast\nالطَّرِيقَةِThe right way, religion of Islam\nغَدَقًاAbundant\nصَعَدًاArduous\nCrowding on top of each other in order to hear him (ﷺ) reciting the Quranلِبَدًا\nيُجِيرَنِيProtect me"],[574,"§Al-Muzzammil\ndeeds\nStrive to pray eleven Rak'a tonight.\nRecite ten verses from the Quran today with precise articulation and intonation (Tajweed), and learn the points of pausing.\nSay, \"Allah is Sufficient for me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.\"\nguid\nBe keen to connect with Allah at all times.\nEndure annoyance patiently.\nThe Day of Resurrection is full of immense terrors.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡمُزَّمِّلُ ١\nAddressing the Prophet (ﷺ) by such description has two benefits, first: Kindness, as when an Arab wants to be friendly with another, he calls him by a name inspired by his current situation. Second: A notice to every person who is wrapped in his bed sleeping to arise to pray at night and remember Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 21/316.\nWhat is secret behind addressing the Prophet (ﷺ) by (O you who wraps himself)?\nنِّصۡفَهُۥٓ أَوِ ٱنقُصۡ مِنۡهُ قَلِيلًا ٣ أَوۡ زِدۡ عَلَيۡهِ\nIf someone asks: When Allah enjoins reducing the time of the nighttime prayer, the statement (or a little less) is used, but when He enjoins the increase, the statement (or add to it) was used, and did not say \"a little,\" but left it open? The answer is: For the increase, abundance is better, but in reduction, there has to be a limit, otherwise it may end up much less than half the night. Ibn Juzay: 2/501.\nReduction is limited while increasing is open. Why?\nوَرَتِّلِ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ تَرۡتِيلًا ٤\nReciting is reading slowly and distinctly with precise articulation points of the letters, which helps to reflect on the meanings of the Quran, unlike one who skims through the Quran without comprehending anything. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to recite every verse separately and distinctly; when he came to a verse that spoke of mercy, he stopped and made supplication, and when he came to a verse that spoke of punishment, he stopped and sought refuge with Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/501.\nWhat is the benefit of reciting the Quran with measured recitation?\nإِنَّ نَاشِئَةَ ٱلَّيۡلِ هِيَ أَشَدُّ وَطۡـٔٗا وَأَقۡوَمُ قِيلًا ٦\nMeaning: The night helps the mind focus on reciting and understanding more than worship during the daytime. This is because the daytime is the time for people to disperse and move about, and be noisy with matters of livelihood. Ibn Kathir: 4/436.\nWhat distinguishes the Quran recitation during the night from that during the day?\nوَٱذۡكُرِ ٱسۡمَ رَبِّكَ وَتَبَتَّلۡ إِلَيۡهِ تَبۡتِيلٗا ٨\nIn the Arabic text, the word used for (devote yourself completely to Him) is “Tabteela,” which indicates: Progression, indulgence in effort, abundance, and intensiveness. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/212.\nWhat is the lesson learned from: (devote yourself completely to Him)?\nوَذَرۡنِي وَٱلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ أُوْلِي ٱلنَّعۡمَةِ وَمَهِّلۡهُمۡ قَلِيلًا ١١\nAllah describes them as (those of ease in life) to rebuke them, for they denied the truth because they were insolent and deluded by their luxurious life. Moreover, this is a warning to them that the One Who says, (And leave to Me the deniers) will remove their life of luxury. Ibn Ashur: 29/269.\nWhat is learned from describing the deniers as: (those of ease in life)?\nإِنَّآ أَرۡسَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكُمۡ رَسُولٗا شَٰهِدًا عَلَيۡكُمۡ كَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَآ إِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ رَسُولٗا ١٥\nThe example of Pharaoh against Moses (u) is chosen for the people of Makkah due to the similarity between them and the people of Egypt in worshiping other than Allah, and their arrogant attitude toward the Messenger who was sent to them, which led them to turn away from the Message that he brought them. Ibn Ashur: 29/273.\nThe example of Pharaoh against Moses (u) is chosen for the people of Makkah. Why?\nwords\nالمُزَّمِّلُThe one who is wrapped in his garment\nوَرَتِّلِRead slowly with precise articulation and clear pauses\nوَتَبَتَّلDevote yourself to worshiping Him\nأُولِي النَّعمَةِThose who have a life of luxury\nأَنكَالًاHeavy shackles\nذَا غُصَّةٍFood that chokes\nتَرجُفُConvulse\nكَثِيبًاDunes\nمَهِيلًاLoose sand\nوَبِيلًاSevere"],[575,"§Al-Muzzammil, Al-Muddaththir\ndeeds\nEnsure to pray three rak'a tonight.\nPerform the five daily prayers in congregation.\nInform a Muslim that purifying garments is liked by Allah.\nguid\nAllah intends ease for His servants and mercy for the Ummah.\nCalling to the path of Allah contradicts laziness.\nRemind yourself of the hardships of the Last Day.\nrefl\n۞إِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَعۡلَمُ أَنَّكَ تَقُومُ أَدۡنَىٰ مِن ثُلُثَيِ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَنِصۡفَهُۥ وَثُلُثَهُۥ وَطَآئِفَةٞ مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ مَعَكَۚ\nStarting the verse with: (Indeed, your Lord knows that you [O Prophet] stand up), implies a praise for the Prophet (ﷺ) for carrying out what he was enjoined by Allah, Who cares for him and says: (Half of it, or a little less ` Or add to it), but the Prophet (ﷺ) chose the higher limit, which was nearly two-thirds of the night, as the Messengers of Firm Resolve would. Ibn Ashur: 29/280.\nThe verse starts with: (Indeed, your Lord knows that you [O Prophet] stand up). Why?\nعَلِمَ أَن سَيَكُونُ مِنكُم مَّرۡضَىٰ وَءَاخَرُونَ يَضۡرِبُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يَبۡتَغُونَ مِن فَضۡلِ ٱللَّهِ وَءَاخَرُونَ يُقَٰتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۖ\nAllah mentions their excuses, saying: (He knows that there are some among you who will be ill) so they cannot pray at night; (and others traveling in the land, seeking the bounty of Allah), which means that they travel for business and profits, and seek what they need from the grace of Allah for their livelihood, so they cannot pray at night; (and others fighting in Allah's way), the mujahideen, so they cannot pray at night. Allah mentions three reasons for waiving the obligation of nighttime prayer, and for these reasons, He waived it for the rest of Muslim Ummah. Al-Shawkani: 5/322.\nThis verse mentions excuses for waiving the obligation of nighttime prayer. What are they?\nوَٱسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ ٱللَّهَۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمُۢ ٢٠\nThe statement: (All-Forgiving, Most-Merciful) serves as a basis for seeking forgiveness, which means: Seek forgiveness because Allah is abundantly Forgiving and intensely Merciful. The aim behind this rationale is encouragement and inducement to seek forgiveness, as it will hopefully be answered. The mention of these two of Allah's Names that are in emphasized form is an indication of a promise of answer. Ibn Ashur: 29/290.\nThe verse is concluded by, (for indeed Allah is All-Forgiving, Most-Merciful). Why?\nوَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرۡ ٤\nOr it may be that what is meant by garments is garments in the usual sense, and that he was commanded to purify them and remove all impurities from them, at all times, especially when beginning to pray. As he was enjoined to purify himself outwardly, then outward purification is part of inward purification. Al-Saadi: 895.\nThe command to purify the garments indicates inward purification. How?\nوَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرۡ ٤\n(And purify your garments), Muhammad bin Sirin said: Wash them with water. Ibn Zaid said: The polytheists were not used to purifying [anything], hence, Allah commanded His Prophet (ﷺ) to purify himself and his garments. Al-Tabari: 23/12.\nWhat is meant by: (And purify your garments)?\nفَذَٰلِكَ يَوۡمَئِذٖ يَوۡمٌ عَسِيرٌ ٩ عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ غَيۡرُ يَسِيرٖ ١٠\nAl-Zamakhshari said: (Not easy) could have been sufficed by (a difficult day), but this is to indicate that this difficulty will not be eased similar to what occurs in worldly life, which is a further warning to the disbelievers, and good tidings to the believers because it will be easy for them. Perhaps the two meanings are independent of each other, and (a difficult day) is a distinct description of that day and an illustration of its immense terror. Al-Shanqiti: 8/363.\nHow are these two terms relevant to each other: (difficult), (not easy)?\nوَبَنِينَ شُهُودٗا ١٣\nThey are not absent, which means that they are present with him. They do not travel for business trading. Rather, their servants and hired workers handle all of that for them while they are sitting with their father. He enjoys their company and delights in being with them. This was a great blessing in their living with him. Ibn Kathir: 4/442.\nWhat is the blessing of having one's sons present with him?\nwords\nلَن تُحصُوهُYou will not be able to pray all night\nالمُدَّثِّرُOne who is covered in his garments\nوَالرُّجزَIdols, actions of shirk\nوَلاَ تَمنُن تَستَكثِرُDo not do a favor for a greater return\nنُقِرَ فِي النَّاقُورِWhen the horn is blown for resurrection\nسَأُرهِقُهُ صَعُودًاI will subject him to a severe torment\nوقَدَّرَHe deliberated to discredit the Quran"],[576,"§Al-Muddaththir\ndeeds\nPerform the five daily prayers in congregation.\nFeed a needy person so that you may be saved from the Fire.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from uttering a lie, or committing a wicked act.\" And avoid engaging if false talk, or that of which you have no knowledge.\nguid\nThe angels are greater beings in size.\nAllah may swear by any of His created beings, but man cannot swear except by Allah.\nParadise is the reward for the people of the right.\nrefl\nوَمَا جَعَلۡنَآ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلنَّارِ إِلَّا مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗۖ وَمَا جَعَلۡنَا عِدَّتَهُمۡ إِلَّا فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لِيَسۡتَيۡقِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَيَزۡدَادَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنٗا وَلَا يَرۡتَابَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ وَلِيَقُولَ ٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ مَاذَآ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهُ بِهَٰذَا مَثَلٗاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَهۡدِي مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَمَا يَعۡلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَۚ وَمَا هِيَ إِلَّا ذِكۡرَىٰ لِلۡبَشَرِ ٣١\nWhen the truth comes upon the hearts, they become one of these four types: First: A tested heart that reacts with disbelief and denial. Second: A heart whose faith increases in certainty. Third: A heart whose certainty is assured, and so proof is established against it, Fourth: A heart that becomes bewildered and blind, and does not know what it is. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/216.\nWhen the truth comes upon the hearts, they turn into different types. What are they?\nلِيَسۡتَيۡقِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَيَزۡدَادَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنٗا\nThis affirms that the believer's duty is to hasten to believe and submit to any command or news from Allah, even if he does not know the wisdom or the aim for it, as Allah knows best. Al-Shanqiti: 8/365.\nDoes the believer have to know the wisdom behind every matter in Islam to believe in it?\nوَلَا يَرۡتَابَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ\nMeaning: To dispel doubts from them. These are important objectives to which people of mature understanding pay attention and care about, striving to increase their certainty and faith at all times, with regard to issues of religion, and to ward off doubt and illusion that could undermine the truth in a person's mind. Al-Saadi: 897.\nThis verse indicates that it is an obligation to have certainty in all religious matters. Explain.\nكُلُّ نَفۡسِۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتۡ رَهِينَةٌ ٣٨ إِلَّآ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡيَمِينِ ٣٩\n(Except the People of the Right), those who were described before, for they had sided with Allah, adhered to His commands, and refrained from His prohibitions; they will not be held in pledge for their deeds. Rather, Allah will have mercy toward them; He will accept their good deeds and forgive their sins. Al-Biqai: 21/71.\nWho are the people of the right?\nمَا سَلَكَكُمۡ فِي سَقَرَ ٤٢ قَالُواْ لَمۡ نَكُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُصَلِّينَ ٤٣\nThis indicates that those who are firm in their duty toward prayer will be protected from such fate. Moreover, it shows that praying is the greatest of all good deeds and that prayer will be the first thing for which a person is called to account, on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Biqai: 21/75.\nWhat will be reason for those to enter the Fire? What is the lesson learned from that?\nمَا سَلَكَكُمۡ فِي سَقَرَ ٤٢ قَالُواْ لَمۡ نَكُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُصَلِّينَ ٤٣\nThis verse indicates that a Muslim who neglects establishing prayer and giving zakah will deserve a share of the Fire commensurate with the amount of his negligence, and based on Allah's Judgement of his good deeds and evil ones, and his outward actions and his inward intents. Ibn Ashur: 29/328.\nThis verse indicates the risk for a Muslim to neglect prayer and zakah. Explain.\nوَكُنَّا نَخُوضُ مَعَ ٱلۡخَآئِضِينَ ٤٥\nMeaning: We engaged in falsehood with those who engaged in it. Falsehood refers to inappropriate words and actions, such as revealing intimate talks between a husband and his wife, or immoral talks by evildoers for fun and joy. Al-Alusi: 15/147.\nA loose tongue can be a disaster. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nفَقُتِلَHe was defeated\nنَظَرَHe ponders to discredit the Quran\nعَبَسَHe frowned\nوَبَسَرَHe scowled\nأَدبَرَHe turned away from the truth\nيُؤثَرُFrom the past people\nسَأُصلِيهِ سَقَرَI will make him burn in the Scorching Fire\nلَوَّاحَةٌ لِلبَشَرِBurning and blackening the skins\nمَا سَلَكَكُمWhat has caused you to enter"],[577,"§Al-Muddaththir, Al-Qiyamah\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You to grant me the intercession of Your Prophet (ﷺ).\" And strive for that through good deeds.\nReproach yourself before regretting your actions.\nSay, \"O Allah, forgive me my past and future sins.\"\nguid\nAttend Islamic study circles and sermons, and do not turn away from the Reminder.\nAllah is the One Whose punishment should be feared and Whose forgiveness should be sought.\nSelf-reckoning is important.\nrefl\nفَمَا تَنفَعُهُمۡ شَفَٰعَةُ ٱلشَّٰفِعِينَ ٤٨\nThis indicates that, on the Day of Resurrection, intercession will benefit others in general, and it is detailed in authentic narrations. Ibn Ashur: 29/328.\nWhat does this verse indicate (so the intercession of intercessors will not benefit them)?\nهُوَ أَهۡلُ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ وَأَهۡلُ ٱلۡمَغۡفِرَةِ ٥٦\nHe is worthy to be feared and He is worthy to forgive the sins of whoever turns to Him in repentance. Ibn Kathir: 4/447.\nKnowing that Allah is the most worthy to forgive sins, what should be your position?\nوَلَآ أُقۡسِمُ بِٱلنَّفۡسِ ٱللَّوَّامَةِ ٢\nIt is the self-blaming soul for its sins, or shortcomings. Human souls are three types: The best among them is the tranquil soul, while the worst is the persistent enjoiner of evil; the self-reproaching soul is between them. Ibn Juzay: 2/51.\nWhat is the difference between the soul that is persistent enjoiner of evil and the self-reproaching soul?\nوَلَآ أُقۡسِمُ بِٱلنَّفۡسِ ٱللَّوَّامَةِ ٢\nAllah describes the human soul as reproaching to indicate its extreme need for one who can show it what is good and what is evil, guide it, and inspire it to adhere to good and invite others to it, and refrain from evil and abhor it to eliminate self-reproaching and the evil that leads to it. Since it is reproaching, hesitant, and constantly changing, it needs one to identify what is best for it in this worldly life and the Hereafter so it favors it and becomes blameful when it misses it. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/225.\nWhat is meant by the self-reproaching soul?\nلَا تُحَرِّكۡ بِهِۦ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعۡجَلَ بِهِۦٓ ١٦\nThis implies showing patience and ascertainment when receiving knowledge; the listener should not hasten to acquire the knowledge before the teacher is finished speaking, but display patience until his teacher finishes his talks, then he should repeat what he heard to his teacher, or ask him about things that he could not understand, and should not cut him off before he is done. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/230.\nThis verse teaches an etiquette that students of knowledge should follow. What is it?\nلَا تُحَرِّكۡ بِهِۦ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعۡجَلَ بِهِۦٓ ١٦ إِنَّ عَلَيۡنَا جَمۡعَهُۥ وَقُرۡءَانَهُۥ ١٧ فَإِذَا قَرَأۡنَٰهُ فَٱتَّبِعۡ قُرۡءَانَهُۥ ١٨ ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيۡنَا بَيَانَهُۥ ١٩\nThis verse highlights the etiquette of receiving knowledge; the learner should not hasten to ask questions before the teacher has finished explaining the issue that he started discussing. Then when he has finished, the learner may ask about anything he did not understand. Similarly, if there is something at the beginning that needs to be questioned or approved, one should not hasten to either question it or accept it, until the speaker has finished speaking, so that it may become clear what his words contain truth or falsehood, and so that the listener may understand it in such a way that he can comment on it. Al-Saadi: 899.\nWhat is the etiquette of the student of knowledge learned from this verse?\nإِنَّ عَلَيۡنَا جَمۡعَهُۥ وَقُرۡءَانَهُۥ ١٧\n(It is upon Us its collection and [to make possible] its recitation): This points to the fact that the Quran was revealed over stages, and indicates that the present collection of the Quran is due to Allah's preservation and guardianship, and a manifestation of this verse: (It is upon Us its collection and [to make possible] its recitation). The current form of collection of the Quran is a testimony to its preservation by Allah as He pledged to do so, and Allah knows best. Al-Shanqiti: 8/374.\nThis verse indicates that the Quran was revealed over stages and that its current form of collection is due to Allah's preservation. Explain\nwords\nحُمُرٌFrightened wild donkeys\nقَسوَرَةٍA fierce lion\nاللَّوَّامَةِA self-reproaching soul\nنُسَوِّيَ بَنَانَهُWe restore even his very fingertips\nأَيَّانَWhen?!\nبَرِقَ البَصَرُThe sight will be dazzled\nلاَ وَزَرَThere will be no refuge from Allah except with Him\nالمُستَقَرُّDestination\nوَلَو أَلقَى مَعَاذِيرَهُEven if he presents his excuses, none will be accepted"],[578,"§Al-Qiyamah, Al-Insan\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, let not worldly affairs be my principal concern, or the ultimate limit of my knowledge.\"\nAsk Allah for a good end to your life.\nAsk Allah for guidance.\nguid\nStrive to do good deeds that make the believer among those who will look at Allah.\nReflect on the creation of man.\nFor Fajr prayer on Fridays, remember to read Surat As-Sajdah in first rak'a, and Surat Al-Insan in the second rak'a.\nrefl\nكَلَّا بَلۡ تُحِبُّونَ ٱلۡعَاجِلَةَ ٢٠ وَتَذَرُونَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَ ٢١\nSince the delights and pleasures of this world are immediate, and man is fond of that which is immediate, whereas the eternal bliss of the hereafter is deferred. It is for this reason that you are negligent about the hereafter, and you ignore it as if you were not created for it, and as if this worldly realm were the eternal realm for the sake of which you are spending your precious lives and striving for it night and day. Thus, facts are turned upside down, which results in loss. Al-Saadi: 900.\nWhat is the reason for mankind to love this fleeting world and neglect the Hereafter?\nوَقِيلَ مَنۡۜ رَاقٖ ٢٧\nThat is, anyone who could perform Ruqyah (supplication for healing), because they have lost all hope of regular ways of healing, so there is nothing left but to pursue divine means. Al-Saadi: 900.\nThey look for one to perform Ruqyah instead of looking for a doctor. Why?\nثُمَّ ذَهَبَ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِۦ يَتَمَطَّىٰٓ ٣٣\nMeaning: He swaggered in pride. It is said that he moved slowly, hence he was too slow to respond to the call of truth. Al-Qurtubi: 21/437.\nWhat is the censured walk mentioned in this verse?\nهَلۡ أَتَىٰ عَلَى ٱلۡإِنسَٰنِ حِينٞ مِّنَ ٱلدَّهۡرِ لَمۡ يَكُن شَيۡٔا مَّذۡكُورًا ١\nMaking man's origins known to him so he would realize that he has no right to be arrogant or assume supremacy. Moreover, he should not be deluded by Allah's hidden kindness, care, and honor toward him, and believes that he is entitled to all that and deserved it. The fact remains: (Whatever blessing you have, it is from Allah)[16:53]. Al-Biqai: 21/123.\nWhat induces an ignorant person to be arrogant?\nإِنَّا خَلَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مِن نُّطۡفَةٍ أَمۡشَاجٖ نَّبۡتَلِيهِ فَجَعَلۡنَٰهُ سَمِيعَۢا بَصِيرًا ٢\n(From a drop of mixed fluids), an insignificant fluid that is regarded as off-putting. (In order to test him) thereby, to see whether he would pay attention to how he was in his initial state, or he would forget it and become arrogant. Al-Saadi: 900.\nThis verse shows man how to rid of conceitedness. Explain.\nإِنَّا خَلَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مِن نُّطۡفَةٍ أَمۡشَاجٖ نَّبۡتَلِيهِ فَجَعَلۡنَٰهُ سَمِيعَۢا بَصِيرًا ٢ إِنَّا هَدَيۡنَٰهُ ٱلسَّبِيلَ إِمَّا شَاكِرٗا وَإِمَّا كَفُورًا ٣\nMeaning: We gave him the faculties of hearing and sight so that he would be able to use them for obedience and disobedience. Ibn Kathir: 4/453.\nAllah mentions the faculties of hearing and sight before saying: (Indeed, We showed him the way, whether he is grateful or ungrateful). Why?\nإِنَّا هَدَيۡنَٰهُ ٱلسَّبِيلَ إِمَّا شَاكِرٗا وَإِمَّا كَفُورًا ٣\nIn the Arabic text, the word (grateful) is not emphasized while the word (ungrateful) is, because true gratefulness to Allah cannot be reached, and his gratefulness for Allah's blessings will always be little, hence, the emphasis would not be applicable. Ungratefulness, however, is emphasized to indicate that he is abundantly ungrateful for Allah's blessings and kindness toward him. Al-Qurtubi: 21/450\nIn the Arabic text, the word (grateful) is not emphasized while the word (ungrateful) is. Why?\nwords\nنَاضِرَةٌBright and radiant\nبَاسِرَةٌGloomy\nفَاقِرَةٌA backbreaking calamity\nبَلَغَتِ التَّرَاقِيَThe soul has reached the collar bone\nمَن رَاقٍWho will cure him\nيَتَمَطَّىSwaggering in pride\nسُدىًLeft neglected\nعَلَقَةًA clinging clot\nأَمشَاجٍA drop of mixed fluids"],[579,"§Al-Insan\ndeeds\nWhen you pledge a vow, fulfill it.\nGive a needy person preference over yourself by giving him food of which you love.\nSay the daily morning remembrance before going to school or work, and evening remembrance before sunset.\nguid\nDevote all deeds sincerely to Allah.\nReflect on the bliss in which the people of Paradise will be.\nPatience is one of the signs of being content with Allah's decree and destiny.\nrefl\nيُوفُونَ بِٱلنَّذۡرِ وَيَخَافُونَ يَوۡمٗا كَانَ شَرُّهُۥ مُسۡتَطِيرٗا ٧\nMeaning: They fulfill what they commit themselves to for the sake of Allah. If they fulfill vows, which are not obligatory upon them unless they take that upon themselves, it is more likely that they will fulfill their commitment to basic obligatory duties. Al-Saadi: 901.\nAllah praises the righteous for fulfilling their vows, what does that indicate?\nوَيُطۡعِمُونَ ٱلطَّعَامَ عَلَىٰ حُبِّهِۦ مِسۡكِينٗا وَيَتِيمٗا وَأَسِيرًا ٨ إِنَّمَا نُطۡعِمُكُمۡ لِوَجۡهِ ٱللَّهِ لَا نُرِيدُ مِنكُمۡ جَزَآءٗ وَلَا شُكُورًا ٩\nWhoever asks needy people to supplicate Allah for him or to compliment him, will not be part of this verse. Ibn Taimyah: 6/441.\nWhen will feeding poor people be for Allah's sake only?\nوَجَزَىٰهُم بِمَا صَبَرُواْ جَنَّةٗ وَحَرِيرٗا ١٢\nMeaning: For enduring hunger patiently, and giving others preference over themselves. Ibn Juzay: 2/519.\nIn this verse, what is the trait for which the righteous entered Paradise?\nوَجَزَىٰهُم بِمَا صَبَرُواْ جَنَّةٗ وَحَرِيرٗا ١٢ مُّتَّكِـِٔينَ فِيهَا عَلَى ٱلۡأَرَآئِكِۖ لَا يَرَوۡنَ فِيهَا شَمۡسٗا وَلَا زَمۡهَرِيرٗا ١٣\nSince patience involves holding oneself against what it dislikes and enduring roughness, tiredness, and heat, the reward will be Paradise which has wide spaces, soft silk garments, and reclining that brings comfort, and shades. Ibn Taimyah: 6/44.\nThe bliss of Paradise is based on spaciousness and softness. Why?\n۞وَيَطُوفُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وِلۡدَٰنٞ مُّخَلَّدُونَ إِذَا رَأَيۡتَهُمۡ حَسِبۡتَهُمۡ لُؤۡلُؤٗا مَّنثُورٗا ١٩\nBoys are the best for serving others, as they are light and quick, and because the served person does not shy away from commanding and forbidding them. Ibn Ashur: 29/397.\nBoys will be serving the people of Paradise. Why?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ لِحُكۡمِ رَبِّكَ\nMeaning: Just as you have been honored by what has been revealed to you, then be patient with Allah's decree and decision, and know that He will manage your affairs in a good manner. Ibn Kathir: 4/458.\nWhat is the benefit of linking patience to Allah's decree?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ لِحُكۡمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تُطِعۡ مِنۡهُمۡ ءَاثِمًا أَوۡ كَفُورٗا ٢٤ وَٱذۡكُرِ ٱسۡمَ رَبِّكَ بُكۡرَةٗ وَأَصِيلٗا ٢٥\nMeaning: Be patient in accepting the decree of Allah without complaining about it, and in accepting His religious rulings, and adhere to them, and do not let any obstacle prevent you from doing so. Since worshiping Allah and remembering Him a great deal would help his patience, Allah enjoined that upon him and said: (And mention the name of your Lord [in prayer] morning and even). Al-Saadi: 902.\nAfter enjoining patience, Allah enjoins the mention of His name in the morning and evening. Why?\nwords\nيَشرَبُ بِهَاThey will drink\nمُستَطِيرًاWidespread\nقَمطَرِيرًاVery grim\nالأَرَائِكِAdorned couches\nزَمهَرِيرًاExcessive bitter cold\nوَدَانِيَةًNear branches above them\nوَذُلِّلَت قُطُوفُهَاThey will be made within their reach\nقَوَارِيرَاOf crystal\nتُسَمَّى سَلسَبِيلًاA fountain named Salsabeel because its water flows pleasantly down the throat"],[580,"§Al-Insan, Al-Mursalat\ndeeds\nPerform prayer and glorify Allah often tonight.\nSay: \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He, Glorified is Allah the Great,\" a hundred times.\nAsk Allah to admit you into His mercy.\nguid\nHow vile the people become in the sight of Allah when they disobey Him.\nReflect on the winds and its types.\nThe terrors of the Day of Resurrection are severe.\nrefl\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَٱسۡجُدۡ لَهُۥ وَسَبِّحۡهُ لَيۡلٗا طَوِيلًا ٢٦\nThe mention of prostration to indicate the prayer implies that prostration is the best act in prayer, and the night is the time for submissiveness. Al-Biqai: 21/157.\nThe prayer is referred to as prostration. Why?\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَٱسۡجُدۡ لَهُۥ وَسَبِّحۡهُ لَيۡلٗا طَوِيلًا ٢٦\nMeaning: Prostrate to Him often, and that can only be done by offering many prayers. Al-Saadi: 903.\nThis verse encourages praying at night often. How?\nنَّحۡنُ خَلَقۡنَٰهُمۡ وَشَدَدۡنَآ أَسۡرَهُمۡۖ وَإِذَا شِئۡنَا بَدَّلۡنَآ أَمۡثَٰلَهُمۡ تَبۡدِيلًا ٢٨\n(It is We Who created them) from nothing (and strengthened their build), We made them strong and perfected their creation, with sinews, veins, arteries, and visible and hidden strengths, until their bodies were perfected and completed, and they were able to do anything they wanted. The One Who created them in this manner is able to recreate them after their death to requite them. Al-Saadi: 903.\nMan's life indicates that resurrection is possible on the Last Day. How?\nإِنَّ هَٰذِهِۦ تَذۡكِرَةٞۖ فَمَن شَآءَ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِۦ سَبِيلٗا ٢٩ وَمَا تَشَآءُونَ إِلَّآ أَن يَشَآءَ ٱللَّهُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمٗا ٣٠\n(So let anyone who wills may take a way to his Lord), taking the way to Allah is tied to the will of man, but the will of man is tied to the Will of Allah in the following verse: (But you cannot will unless Allah wills), which is Allah's decree and destiny. Al-Shanqiti: 8/399.\nThese two verses contain one of the pillars of faith. What is it?\nوَٱلۡمُرۡسَلَٰتِ عُرۡفٗا ١ فَٱلۡعَٰصِفَٰتِ عَصۡفٗا ٢ وَٱلنَّٰشِرَٰتِ نَشۡرٗا ٣ فَٱلۡفَٰرِقَٰتِ فَرۡقٗا ٤ فَٱلۡمُلۡقِيَٰتِ ذِكۡرًا ٥\nThe oath is long, keeping the listener in suspense and wanting to know what it is about. Ibn Ashur: 29/419.\nThis Surah contains a long oath. Why?\nوَمَآ أَدۡرَىٰكَ مَا يَوۡمُ ٱلۡفَصۡلِ ١٤\nMeaning: The Day of Judgment is an event worthy of greatness and of being inquired about. All other great events do not compare to it, and none among the creation can ever reach the knowledge of when or how it will manifest because there is nothing like it. Al-Biqai: 21/170.\nWhat does the inquiry in this verse indicate?\nوَيۡلٞ يَوۡمَئِذٖ لِّلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ١٥\nThis is repeated after each verse to divide the punishment commensurate with their denial, where there will be a punishment for each denial. Al-Qurtubi: 21/501-502.\nThis verse is repeated after each verse. Why?\nwords\nفَالعَاصِفَاتِ عَصفًاSwearing by the winds that blow violently\nوَالنَّاشِرَاتِ نَشرًاSwearing by angels that spread clouds\nفَالفَارِقَاتِ فَرقًاSwearing by the angels who bring criterion\nطُمِسَتEffaced\nفُرِجَتSplit apart\nنُسِفَتBlown Away\nأُقِّتَتGiven appointment to testify against their nations"],[581,"§Al-Mursalat\ndeeds\nVisit the cemetery and take heed of that.\nAsk Allah to give you fresh water and send the rain.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Hellfire, three times.\nguid\nReflect on the creation of man, and its indication of resurrection.\nReflect on the shadow of the disbelievers.\nThe doers of good will have a great reward on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ نَجۡعَلِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ كِفَاتًا ٢٥\nThe earth contains the living on top of it and the dead inside it. This proves that burying the dead is obligatory, even its hair when it is cut off and other parts removed from the human body. Al-Qurtubi: 21/505\nWhat is the Sharia ruling learned from this verse?\nإِنَّهَا تَرۡمِي بِشَرَرٖ كَٱلۡقَصۡرِ ٣٢ كَأَنَّهُۥ جِمَٰلَتٞ صُفۡرٞ ٣٣\n(Tawny camels): The word translated here as (tawny) refers to a black color with a hint of yellow. This indicates that the flames, coals, and sparks of hell are dark, and that it is black, terrible in appearance, and extremely hot. We ask Allah to keep us safe from it and from the deeds that would bring us close to it. Al-Saadi: 905.\nThrough your reflection on the meaning of this verse, what is the color of Hellfire? Is it all dark, or does it have some light?\nفَإِن كَانَ لَكُمۡ كَيۡدٞ فَكِيدُونِ ٣٩\nThis highlights their helplessness, alludes to their plans in worldly life, and rebukes them for that. Ibn Juzay: 2/525.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the disbelievers will be helpless and unable to speak, so how can they plan anything?\nكُلُواْ وَٱشۡرَبُواْ هَنِيٓـَٔۢا بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٤٣\nThis proves that their righteous deeds in worldly life will be a reason for them to enjoy the bliss of Paradise in the Hereafter, but a Prophetic Hadith states: \"There is none whose deeds alone would entitle him to get into Paradise.\" There is no contradiction between the two texts, as entering Paradise is by the favor of Allah, and after they enter, their rankings and pleasures will be based on their deeds. Hence, They all share Allah's favor in entering Paradise, but their ranks will vary commensurate with their deeds. Al-Shanqiti: 8/404.\nWhat is the link between righteous deeds and entering Paradise? Explain.\nكُلُواْ وَتَمَتَّعُواْ قَلِيلًا إِنَّكُم مُّجۡرِمُونَ ٤٦\nThis indicates that every criminal will enjoy himself for a few days [in worldly life], but will end up in permanent torment and suffering [in the Hereafter]. Al-Alusi: 15/197.\nWhat is the indication of enjoining the disbelievers to eat and enjoy themselves in this worldly life?\nوَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمُ ٱرۡكَعُواْ لَا يَرۡكَعُونَ ٤٨\nMeaning: Obey Allah, the Almighty, be humble and modest with Him by accepting His revelation and following His religion, and reject this arrogance and conceit. (They do not bow), they do not humble themselves, refuse to accept it, and persist in their arrogance. Al-Alusi: 15/197.\nWhat is the indication of enjoining the polytheists to bow and their refusal to do so?\nوَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمُ ٱرۡكَعُواْ لَا يَرۡكَعُونَ ٤٨ وَيۡلٞ يَوۡمَئِذٖ لِّلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ٤٩\nPart of their evildoing is that when they were enjoined to pray, which is one of the noblest acts of worship, and it was said to them (Bow [in prayer]), they refused to do so. What evildoing can be worse than this? What denial can be greater than this? Al-Saadi: 905.\nDiscuss the importance of prayer in light of this verse.\nwords\nمَاءٍ مَهِينٍWeak fluid, sperm\nقَرَارٍ مَكِينٍA firm lodging, womb\nقَدَرٍA determined time period\nكِفَاتًاA container for the living and the dead\nرَوَاسِيَ شَامِخَاتٍFirm towering mountains\nفُرَاتًاFresh water\nظِلٍّThe smoke of Hellfire\nذِي ثَلاَثِ شُعَبٍAscending in three columns\nلاَ ظَلِيلٍIt does not provide cool shade\nكَالقَصرِA big and tall building structure\nجِمَالَةٌ صُفرٌAs if they were yellowish black camels"],[582,"§An-Naba\ndeeds\nGo to bed early tonight, then draw two benefits from that.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Hellfire, three times.\nRecall a sin that you committed, then ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nAllah's abundant blessings upon His servants entail more gratefulness to Him.\nThe people of the Fire will hope for some coolness and drinks from Paradise until they hear this:\nDenying the reckoning or being heedless of it is a reason for committing more sins.\nrefl\nعَمَّ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ ١ عَنِ ٱلنَّبَإِ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ٢\nAllah mentions their inquiry and that it was about (the momentous news). He presents their query in an interrogative form to attract their attentions and draw their minds to it, then, He explains it in a way that reveals its greatness and immensity; as if saying: What are they asking about? Should I tell you? Then, the answer comes: (About the momentous news). Al-Shawkani: 5/363.\nThis Surah begins with an inquiry. Why?\nٱلَّذِي هُمۡ فِيهِ مُخۡتَلِفُونَ ٣\nAllah says, (they are in disagreement), and did not say, \"they disagreed\" because, in Arabic, the former is a noun clause indicating that their disagreement about this momentous news was continuous and permanent. Ibn Ashur: 30/11.\nIn this verse, a noun clause is used instead of a verbal clause. Why?\nأَلَمۡ نَجۡعَلِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ مِهَٰدٗا ٦ وَٱلۡجِبَالَ أَوۡتَادٗا ٧ وَخَلَقۡنَٰكُمۡ أَزۡوَٰجٗا ٨ وَجَعَلۡنَا نَوۡمَكُمۡ سُبَاتٗا ٩ وَجَعَلۡنَا ٱلَّيۡلَ لِبَاسٗا ١٠ وَجَعَلۡنَا ٱلنَّهَارَ مَعَاشٗا ١١ وَبَنَيۡنَا فَوۡقَكُمۡ سَبۡعٗا شِدَادٗا ١٢ وَجَعَلۡنَا سِرَاجٗا وَهَّاجٗا ١٣ وَأَنزَلۡنَا مِنَ ٱلۡمُعۡصِرَٰتِ مَآءٗ ثَجَّاجٗا ١٤\nAllah, the Almighty, mentions these superlative and inimitable creatures as an argument against their denial of resurrection; as if saying: The God Who created these great creatures is surely capable of resurrecting people after death. Ibn Juzay: 1/2541\nAllah mentions these great creatures to make a point. Explain.\nوَجَعَلۡنَا نَوۡمَكُمۡ سُبَاتٗا ٩\nMeaning: So that you may cease your work which, if you did not stop, would cause you physical harm, hence, Allah has caused the night and sleep to overtake people, so that their harmful physical activities may cease and they may attain some needed rest. Al-Saadi: 906.\nSleep is a blessing from Allah upon His servants. How?\nإِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ كَانَتۡ مِرۡصَادٗا ٢١\nMeaning: No one will enter Paradise until he passes over the Hellfire. If he has what it takes to pass, he will be saved, otherwise he will be held back. Ibn Kathir: 4/464.\nWhat is understood from this verse?\nوَكُلَّ شَيۡءٍ أَحۡصَيۡنَٰهُ كِتَٰبٗا ٢٩\nSmall and great, good and evil, (in a record), which means that We have recorded it in the Preserved Tablet, so the evildoers should not be concerned that We will punish them for sins that they never did, or think that any of their deeds will go to waste or that even an atom's weight of them will be forgotten. Al-Saadi: 907.\nWhat is the wisdom behind recording the servants' deeds?\nفَذُوقُواْ فَلَن نَّزِيدَكُمۡ إِلَّا عَذَابًا ٣٠\nAbdulla bin Amr said: No verse was revealed about the dwellers of the Fire more intense than this (So taste, and never will We increase you except in torment) so, they will be in more torment forever. Al-Tabari: 24/169.\nWhat is the most intense verse about the dwellers of the Fire?\nwords\nسُبَاتًاFor your rest\nسِرَاجًا وَهَّاجًاA blazing lamp\nالمُعصِرَاتِRainclouds\nثَجَّاجًاAbundant water\nوَجَنَّاتٍ أَلفَافًاGardens of entwined growth\nمِيقَاتًاAn appointed time for judgement\nمِرصَادًاLying in wait\nأَحقَابًاEndless ages\nوَغَسَّاقًاDischarge of wounds\nوِفَاقًاA fitting [recompense]"],[583,"§An-Naba, An-Nazi'at\ndeeds\nOn a given day, perform three deeds that indicate righteousness such as fasting, abstaining from sins in fear of Allah, and making a Muslim's heart happy through charity.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil end of life.\nAsk Allah for a good end of life, and remember this verse:\nguid\nThe virtue of righteousness is great, and so is its reward with Allah.\nRevere Allah His true reverence.\nThe Day of Resurrection is near, as every awaited event is near.\nrefl\nلَّا يَسۡمَعُونَ فِيهَا لَغۡوٗا وَلَا كِذَّٰبٗا ٣٥\nThis is similar to this verse, (Free from any vain talk, and free from sin)[52:23]. Meaning: There will not be any vain, worthless speech therein, nor any sinful lying. Rather, it will be the abode of peace, and everything in it will be free of any shortcomings. Ibn Kathir: 4/465.\nThis verse mentions a type of intrapersonal bliss. Explain.\nلَّا يَسۡمَعُونَ فِيهَا لَغۡوٗا وَلَا كِذَّٰبٗا ٣٥\nWhile the immense pain inflicted by the Fire on the senses of its dwellers through burning their bodies and giving them to drink scalding water and foul purulence, so that the torment will be internal as well as external, Allah prevents the least amount of annoyance from reaching the dwellers of the Paradise, which is what people do not like to hear; and that is the least amount of annoyance. Ibn Ashur: 30/46.\nThis verse precludes the dwellers of Paradise from hearing vain talk and lies. How does this pertain to the preceding verses?\nإِنَّآ أَنذَرۡنَٰكُمۡ عَذَابٗا قَرِيبٗا يَوۡمَ يَنظُرُ ٱلۡمَرۡءُ مَا قَدَّمَتۡ يَدَاهُ وَيَقُولُ ٱلۡكَافِرُ يَٰلَيۡتَنِي كُنتُ تُرَٰبَۢا ٤٠\n(Oh, I wish that I were dust), that is what the disbeliever will say on the Day of Resurrection when no repentance will be accepted nor a good deed will avail anything. However, those who say this in worldly life because of their fear of Allah will be rewarded for it, as Mary (o) said: (Oh, I wish I had died before this and was in oblivion, forgotten). This is not the same as wishing for death on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Taimyah: 6/456.\nWhat is the difference between regretting a sin in worldly life and the Hereafter?\nإِنَّآ أَنذَرۡنَٰكُمۡ عَذَابٗا قَرِيبٗا يَوۡمَ يَنظُرُ ٱلۡمَرۡءُ مَا قَدَّمَتۡ يَدَاهُ وَيَقُولُ ٱلۡكَافِرُ يَٰلَيۡتَنِي كُنتُ تُرَٰبَۢا ٤٠\nAbu Huraira and Ibn Omar (j) said: On the Day of Resurrection, retribution will be carried out among animals, then, Allah will say to them: Be dust, and they will. Thereupon, the disbeliever will wish the same. Indeed, the Day of Judgment is of immense greatness and surely inevitable. Al-Biqai: 21/216.\nWhen will the disbeliever wish to be dust? Why would he wish for that?\nوَٱلنَّٰشِطَٰتِ نَشۡطٗا ٢\nSome of the righteous predecessors said: The angels ease out the souls of the believers and let them rest for a while, then, they remove them gently, like a swimmer in the water, moving slowly so he would not drown. They remove the soul softly so that the believer would not feel pain or hardship. Al-Alusi: 30/23.\nExplain how the angels take the souls of the believers. Why?\nقُلُوبٞ يَوۡمَئِذٖ وَاجِفَةٌ ٨ أَبۡصَٰرُهَا خَٰشِعَةٞ ٩\n(Their eyes humbled): This is a metaphor for humiliation and fear. Ibn Juzay: 1/2545.\nIn this verse, the eyes are described as humbled, what does that indicate?\nهَلۡ أَتَىٰكَ حَدِيثُ مُوسَىٰٓ ١٥\nThis is a consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ). Meaning: Pharaoh was more powerful than the disbelievers of your time, but We punished him, and thus will do to these disbelievers. Al-Qurtubi: 22/53.\nAllah relates the story of Moses and Pharaoh to His Prophet (ﷺ). Why?\nwords\nمَفَازًاSalvation, attaining Paradise\nوَكَوَاعِبَYoung women\nدِهَاقًاA full cup of wine\nمَآبًاA way to His Lord through good deeds\nوَالنَّاشِطَاتِAngels who ease out the souls of the believers\nوَالسَّابِحَاتِAngels who glorify Allah on their ascension and descension\nفَالسَّابِقَاتِAngels who race to deliver the revelation to the Prophet\nتَتبَعُهَا الرَّادِفَةُThe second Blast for resurrection"],[584,"§An-Nazi'at\ndeeds\nInvite a non-Muslim to Islam using a wise approach.\nDo a righteous deed that you would love to remember on the Day of Resurrection.\nReckon with yourself before going to bed.\nguid\nWhen inviting others to the way of Allah, a good and soft approach should be used.\nThe excessive tyranny of a person should not keep you from preaching to him.\nBeing conscious of Allah's presence in your life is a great stage.\nrefl\nفَقُلۡ هَل لَّكَ إِلَىٰٓ أَن تَزَكَّىٰ ١٨\nMoses (u) urged Pharaoh to rid himself of false belief, which is a figurative impurity inside the soul, and accept the guidance of one who would lead him to what is good and pure. Ibn Ashur: 30/77.\nAt the outset, Moses (u) urged Pharaoh to purify himself. Why?\nوَأَهۡدِيَكَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَتَخۡشَىٰ ١٩\nIn this verse, (so you would fear) is made as a result of (let me guide you) to indicate that true fear of Allah does not occur without knowledge. Allah says, (Only the people of knowledge among His servants fear Allah)[35:28]. Meaning: Those who know Him have full fear of Him without a mistakes or shortcomings. Ibn Ashur: 30/77.\nIn this verse, the fear of Allah comes as a result of guidance. Why?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَعِبۡرَةٗ لِّمَن يَخۡشَىٰٓ ٢٦\nThe one who fears Allah is the one who will benefit from signs and lessons. When he sees the punishment of Pharaoh, he will realize that whoever is arrogant and disobeys, and opposes the Sovereign Most High, He will punish him in this world and the Hereafter. As for the one whose heart is devoid of fear of Allah, no matter what sign comes to him, he will not believe in it. Al-Saadi: 909.\nWho benefits from the Quranic admonishments? Who does not?\nءَأَنتُمۡ أَشَدُّ خَلۡقًا أَمِ ٱلسَّمَآءُۚ بَنَىٰهَا ٢٧ رَفَعَ سَمۡكَهَا فَسَوَّىٰهَا ٢٨ وَأَغۡطَشَ لَيۡلَهَا وَأَخۡرَجَ ضُحَىٰهَا ٢٩ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَعۡدَ ذَٰلِكَ دَحَىٰهَآ ٣٠ أَخۡرَجَ مِنۡهَا مَآءَهَا وَمَرۡعَىٰهَا ٣١ وَٱلۡجِبَالَ أَرۡسَىٰهَا ٣٢ مَتَٰعٗا لَّكُمۡ وَ لِأَنۡعَٰمِكُمۡ ٣٣\nAllah states that giving a clear sign to those who disbelieve in the resurrection and think it is unlikely that Allah will recreate their bodies: (Are you), O humans, (more difficult to create, or the heaven). The One Who created the mighty heavens and all that they contain of lights and heavenly bodies, and the solid earth and all that it contains of necessities and that which benefits people, will inevitably resurrect those who are accountable, then He will requite them for their deeds. Al-Saadi: 909.\nWhat do these great signs, mentioned by Allah, indicate? Why is the recompense mentioned afterward?\nوَبُرِّزَتِ ٱلۡجَحِيمُ لِمَن يَرَىٰ ٣٦\nThe Fire will be visible to all. As for the believer, seeing the Fire will make him appreciate the immense blessing of Allah on him by saving him from it. For the disbeliever, however, this will add distress to his distress and regrets to his regrets. Al-Shawkani: 5/380.\nWill the Fire be visible to all, or only to the disbelievers? Why?\nوَأَمَّا مَنۡ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهِۦ وَنَهَى ٱلنَّفۡسَ عَنِ ٱلۡهَوَىٰ ٤٠ فَإِنَّ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ هِيَ ٱلۡمَأۡوَىٰ ٤١\nIn the Arabic text, the word for desires is \"Hawa,\" which means inclination, and it is commonly associated with lust. Ar-Raghib said: \"Hawa\" is named as such because it throws those who follow it into disgrace in worldly life and into the abyss in the Hereafter. Those who oppose their \"Hawa\" are therefore praised. A wise man said: If you want to do the right thing, check your \"Hawa,\" and do the opposite. Al-Fudhail said: The best deeds are doing the opposite of your \"Hawa\". Al-Alusi: 30/36.\nWhy is \"Hawa\" named as such?\nإِنَّمَآ أَنتَ مُنذِرُ مَن يَخۡشَىٰهَا ٤٥\nMeaning: You are sent to warn people about it; it is not your duty to inform them when it will occur. (Those who fear it) are singled out because they are the only ones who benefit from the warning. Ibn Juzay: 2/535.\nWho benefits from the warning?\nwords\nتَزَكَّىPurify yourself from disbelief\nوَأَهدِيَكَI guide you\nنَكَالَA punishment\nرَفَعَ سَمكَهَاRaised its ceiling\nوَأَغطَشَ لَيلَهَاDarkened its night\nوَأَخرَجَ ضُحَاهَاBrought forth it daylight\nدَحَاهَاSpread it out\nالطَّامَّةُSecond Blast marking Day of Resurrection\nوَبُرِّزَتِIt will be exposed\nأَيَّانَ مُرسَاهَاWhen will it be\nعَشِيَّةًThe time from noon to sunset"],[585,"§Abasa\ndeeds\nPay a visit, today, to a disabled or a weak person to please him.\nIdentify a time when supplication is likely to be answered and invoke Allah often to guide and forgive your family members.\nSelect a food item today, and reflect on the phases of Allah's creation through which it went before reaching you, then thank Allah for that.\nguid\nThe fact that Allah's gentle reproach of His Prophet is still being recited is one of the great proofs of his truthfulness (ﷺ), and that this Holy Quran is indeed from Allah.\nThank Allah for the diversity of His blessings.\nBe ready for the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nعَبَسَ وَتَوَلَّىٰٓ ١ أَن جَآءَهُ ٱلۡأَعۡمَىٰ ٢ وَمَا يُدۡرِيكَ لَعَلَّهُۥ يَزَّكَّىٰٓ ٣ أَوۡ يَذَّكَّرُ فَتَنفَعَهُ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰٓ ٤ أَمَّا مَنِ ٱسۡتَغۡنَىٰ ٥ فَأَنتَ لَهُۥ تَصَدَّىٰ ٦ وَمَا عَلَيۡكَ أَلَّا يَزَّكَّىٰ ٧ وَأَمَّا مَن جَآءَكَ يَسۡعَىٰ ٨ وَهُوَ يَخۡشَىٰ ٩ فَأَنتَ عَنۡهُ تَلَهَّىٰ ١٠\nThis is a great benefit; it is the purpose for which the Messengers were sent and for which preachers exhort and remind, so if you had turned to and focused your attention on the one who came by himself, seeking that from you, that would have been more appropriate. As for your turning and focusing your attention on the rich man who does not care and does not want to ask or find out anything because of his lack of desire for good, while ignoring the one who is more important than him, that was inappropriate. You are not to be blamed if he does not want to be purified, for you are not to be held accountable for what evil he does. This lends support to the well-known principle that says: Do not abandon that which will lead to a definite interest for something that is merely speculative, and do not give up what definitely could serve a purpose for that which may or may not serve a purpose. Al-Saadi: 911.\nThese verses contain some benefits for the preacher in setting priorities in his preaching. Explain.\nوَأَمَّا مَن جَآءَكَ يَسۡعَىٰ ٨ وَهُوَ يَخۡشَىٰ ٩ فَأَنتَ عَنۡهُ تَلَهَّىٰ ١٠\nThe forbidden action here was turning away from one who accepted Islam, not the approach to another with care by the Prophet (ﷺ) in hope that he would accept Islam. Al-Alusi: 15/243.\nWhat was forbidden action in the story with Ibn Umm Maktoum when he came to the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nكَلَّآ إِنَّهَا تَذۡكِرَةٞ ١١ فَمَن شَآءَ ذَكَرَهُۥ ١٢ فِي صُحُفٖ مُّكَرَّمَةٖ ١٣ مَّرۡفُوعَةٖ مُّطَهَّرَةِۢ ١٤ بِأَيۡدِي سَفَرَةٖ ١٥ كِرَامِۢ بَرَرَةٖ ١٦\n(No indeed; this is a reminder), the Quran. (Preserved) in the hands of angel-scribes ` Noble and dutiful), they are noble, handsome, and honorable in their creation. Their character and their deeds are righteous, pure and perfect. From this, it should be noted that the bearer of the Quran should be following righteousness and guidance in his words and actions. Ibn Kathir: 4/472.\nAllah describes the angels who preserve the pages of the Quran with certain attributes. How can the bearer of the Quran benefit from these attributes?\nمِنۡ أَيِّ شَيۡءٍ خَلَقَهُۥ ١٨ مِن نُّطۡفَةٍ خَلَقَهُۥ فَقَدَّرَهُۥ ١٩\nMeaning: From what substance did Allah create this disbeliever that made him arrogant? Meaning: This is something to wonder about. (From a drop of semen), from a weak insignificant fluid, hence, why does he lose sight of himself? Alhasan said: How can someone who exited through urine passage twice become arrogant? Al-Qurtubi: 22/79.\nThe son of Adam has no right to be arrogant. Why?\nثُمَّ أَمَاتَهُۥ فَأَقۡبَرَهُۥ ٢١\nAllah has honored man with burial and has not made him like all other animals, whose carcasses are left on the face of the earth. Al-Saadi: 911.\nThe burial of man after death is a blessing from Allah. How?\nمِنۡ أَيِّ شَيۡءٍ خَلَقَهُۥ ١٨ مِن نُّطۡفَةٍ خَلَقَهُۥ فَقَدَّرَهُۥ ١٩ ثُمَّ ٱلسَّبِيلَ يَسَّرَهُۥ ٢٠ ثُمَّ أَمَاتَهُۥ فَأَقۡبَرَهُۥ ٢١\nFrom this, it is clear that the beginning of man is a seeded sperm, then he ends up as a rotten corpse, while inholding feces throughout his life. No one honors man with knowledge except the One Who created and perfected his form, hence, this makes it obligatory for him to thank Allah and not be ungrateful. Al-Biqai: 21/262.\nHow does a person become honored and reach a high rank?\nفَلۡيَنظُرِ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ إِلَىٰ طَعَامِهِۦٓ ٢٤\nThis is a command to reflect on food; how it is created by the might of Allah and made available by His mercy, hence, the servant must obey and give thanks to Him. Being disobedient and ungrateful to Allah is indeed abhorrent. Ibn Juzay: 2/538.\nWhat is the lesson learned by the servant when reflecting on Allah's creation?\nwords\nسَفَرَةٍMessenger-angels between Allah and His servants\nنُطفَةٍA drop of weak fluid, semen\nفَقَدَّرَهُHe created him in stages\nأَنشَرَهُHe will resurrect him\nوَقَضبًاFodder for the livestock\nغُلبًاBig dense trees\nوَأَبًّاGrass for the livestock"],[586,"§At-Takwir, Abasa\ndeeds\nBe compassionate toward those who are younger than you.\nDo a righteous deed today that you wish to see it brought before you on the Day of Resurrection.\nAsk Allah for steadfastness on the right path.\nguid\nRemember the Day of Reckoning and be ready for it.\nAllah's honor upon the angels calls the servant to love and believe in them.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) does not know the unseen, and surely neither do those who are below him.\nrefl\nوَوُجُوهٞ يَوۡمَئِذٍ عَلَيۡهَا غَبَرَةٞ ٤٠ تَرۡهَقُهَا قَتَرَةٌ ٤١ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡكَفَرَةُ ٱلۡفَجَرَةُ ٤٢\nMeaning: Those who went beyond the pale of religion until they became firmly entrenched in disbelief and wickedness are mostly the affluent ones whose wealth induced them to become arrogant, insolent, and boastful. They combined disbelief and wickedness, and therefore, they will be requited with dust-stained faces and darkness. Al-Biqai: 21/273.\nThe disbelievers will be requited with dust-stained faces and darkness. Why?\nإِذَا ٱلشَّمۡسُ كُوِّرَتۡ ١ وَإِذَا ٱلنُّجُومُ ٱنكَدَرَتۡ ٢ وَإِذَا ٱلۡجِبَالُ سُيِّرَتۡ ٣ وَإِذَا ٱلۡعِشَارُ عُطِّلَتۡ ٤ وَإِذَا ٱلۡوُحُوشُ حُشِرَتۡ ٥ وَإِذَا ٱلۡبِحَارُ سُجِّرَتۡ ٦ وَإِذَا ٱلنُّفُوسُ زُوِّجَتۡ ٧ وَإِذَا ٱلۡمَوۡءُۥدَةُ سُئِلَتۡ ٨ بِأَيِّ ذَنۢبٖ قُتِلَتۡ ٩ وَإِذَا ٱلصُّحُفُ نُشِرَتۡ ١٠ وَإِذَا ٱلسَّمَآءُ كُشِطَتۡ ١١ وَإِذَا ٱلۡجَحِيمُ سُعِّرَتۡ ١٢ وَإِذَا ٱلۡجَنَّةُ أُزۡلِفَتۡ ١٣ عَلِمَتۡ نَفۡسٞ مَّآ أَحۡضَرَتۡ ١٤\nThese details that Allah gives of the Day of Resurrection form a description that will shake people to the core; hardship will become very intense, people will be deeply shaken and fear will become widespread. This should motivate people of understanding to prepare for that day and deter them from anything that could incur blame. Al-Saadi: 912.\nWhat is the practical benefit you gain from reading these verses?\nوَإِذَا ٱلنُّفُوسُ زُوِّجَتۡ ٧\nEvery person will be paired with another of similar deeds. Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be paired in Paradise, while others who love obeying the devil will be paired in Hellfire. Everyone will be with those whom he loves willingly or unwillingly. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/257.\nYour love for others will make a big difference on the Day of Resurrection. Explain.\nوَإِذَا ٱلۡمَوۡءُۥدَةُ سُئِلَتۡ ٨ بِأَيِّ ذَنۢبٖ قُتِلَتۡ ٩\nThis is an indication that she had no sin for which to be killed, rather, the sin is her killer's, but due to the enormity of the sin, the question will be directed to her as a rebuke to her father. Al-Shanqiti: 8/438.\nThe baby girl will be questioned even though she has no sin. Why?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَقَوۡلُ رَسُولٖ كَرِيمٖ ١٩ ذِي قُوَّةٍ عِندَ ذِي ٱلۡعَرۡشِ مَكِينٖ ٢٠ مُّطَاعٖ ثَمَّ أَمِينٖ ٢١\nAll of this is indicative of the noble status of the Quran before Allah, for it was sent with this noble angel who possesses these perfect characteristics. Usually, kings do not send someone dear to them except on the most important missions and with the most sublime messages. Al-Saadi: 913.\nReflect on the status of the Quran through the attributes of the angel who came down with it to the Prophet (ﷺ).\nوَمَا هُوَ بِقَوۡلِ شَيۡطَٰنٖ رَّجِيمٖ ٢٥ فَأَيۡنَ تَذۡهَبُونَ ٢٦ إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكۡرٞ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٧\nWhoever knew these descriptions of the Quran and that of the two Messengers, the angel and the human, would surely love the Quran and the Messengers. He would immensely revere the Quran, recite it all the time, strive to follow its commands and refrain from its prohibitions to be steadfast on the right path with the aim to enjoy the company of the one who conveyed it and seeing the One Whom it came from. Al-Biqai: 21/294.\nWhat is the benefit of knowing descriptions of the Quran and that of the Messengers who conveyed it?\nإِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكۡرٞ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٧ لِمَن شَآءَ مِنكُمۡ أَن يَسۡتَقِيمَ ٢٨\nMeaning: This Quran is a reminder for all of mankind. They are reminded by it and receive admonition from it. (For whoever wills among you to take a right path), whoever seeks guidance, must adhere to this Quran, for verily it is his salvation and guidance, and no guidance in anything else. Ibn Kathir: 4/481.\nPresently, mankind try to look for a straight path of salvation away from the darkness of misguidance. What is the only way to true guidance and salvation?\nwords\nقَتَرَةٌHumiliation and darkness\nانكَدَرَتFall down and their light vanish\nالعِشَارُFull-term pregnant she-camels\nعُطِّلَتNeglected\nسُجِّرَتFilled with flame\nالمَوءُودَةُThe baby girl buried alive\nكُشِطَتStripped away\nأُزلِفَتBrought near"],[587,"§Al-Infitar, Al-Mutaffifin\ndeeds\nVisit the graves.\nThank Allah, the Almighty, for your body's good creation.\nRecall a sin you committed and ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nHasten to do good deeds and do not take Allah's forbearance for granted.\nThe good creation of man's body is a blessing from Allah.\nEvery deed you do is recorded either for you or against you.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ ٱلۡكَرِيمِ ٦\n(Your Lord, the Most Generous) This phrase also indicates that His retribution will be carried out when wickedness is excessive, as the lord would do. This would prevent being deceived concerning Him for those who reflect. Al-Biqai: 21/302.\nWhat is the indication of saying (Your Lord, the Most Generous)?\nوَإِنَّ عَلَيۡكُمۡ لَحَٰفِظِينَ ١٠ كِرَامٗا كَٰتِبِينَ ١١ يَعۡلَمُونَ مَا تَفۡعَلُونَ ١٢\nAllah has appointed you noble angels who record your words and deeds, and they know all that you do. Hence, what is appropriate on your part is to honor and respect them. Al-Saadi: 914.\nWhat is your feeling toward the angels who record your deeds? To what does this feeling lead you?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡأَبۡرَارَ لَفِي نَعِيمٖ ١٣\nAs a reward for them, their hearts, spirits and bodies will be a state of bliss in this world, in the intermediate life (al-Barzakh), and the abode of eternity. Al-Saadi: 914.\nObedience to Allah results in a blissful life over three stages through which man pass. What are they?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡأَبۡرَارَ لَفِي نَعِيمٖ ١٣ وَإِنَّ ٱلۡفُجَّارَ لَفِي جَحِيمٖ ١٤\nThese verses are not limited to the bliss and torment in the Hereafter only, rather, it is in all stages of their lives: Worldly life, the intermediate life (al-Barzakh), and the eternal abode. One party will be in bliss and the other in torment. True bliss and true torment are that of the heart. No torment is more severe than feeling fear, distress, grief, sadness, turning away from Allah and the Hereafter, and being attached to other than Allah. When one becomes attached to a person or a thing and loves them besides Allah, they will be a source of dreadful torment upon him. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/267.\nIn what life will the bliss and torment, mentioned in the verses, occur?\nوَيۡلٞ لِّلۡمُطَفِّفِينَ ١\nOpening this Surah with a threat to the defrauders indicates the immense consequence of this behavior. Fraud is a true risk because fairness is the basis of the world economy and the balance of business dealings, hence, any disruption to it will result in wide corruption. Al-Shanqiti: 8/454.\nWhat is the benefit of opening this Surah with a threat to the defrauders?\nوَيۡلٞ لِّلۡمُطَفِّفِينَ ١ ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ٱكۡتَالُواْ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ يَسۡتَوۡفُونَ ٢ وَإِذَا كَالُوهُمۡ أَو وَّزَنُوهُمۡ يُخۡسِرُونَ ٣\nThis points to the fact that evil behavior is the cause of corruption, which is love for worldly gains, manifested in the avidity for gathering wealth unlawfully even through the lowest of schemes such as defrauding in measure and weight. Al-Biqai: 21/311.\nWhat is the cause of corruption? How is linked to defrauding in measure and weight?\nأَلَا يَظُنُّ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَنَّهُم مَّبۡعُوثُونَ ٤ لِيَوۡمٍ عَظِيمٖ ٥ يَوۡمَ يَقُومُ ٱلنَّاسُ لِرَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٦\nThese verses contain interrogative and exclamatory sentences, using the word (think), describing the Last Day as (tremendous), the standing of people submissively before Allah, and describing Himself as the Lord of the worlds. This is an eloquent explanation of the gravity of the sin of defrauding in measure and weight. Al-Qurtubi: 22/136.\nDefrauding is considered a grave sin by Allah. How?\nwords\nانفَطَرَتBreaks apart\nانتَثَرَتFallen and scattered\nفُجِّرَتOverflowed and burst forth\nبُعثِرَتOverturned and its contents scattered\nمَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَWhat has deceived you concerning your Lord to disobey Him\nفَسَوَّاكَHe shaped you\nفَعَدَلَكَHe proportioned you\nلَحَافِظِينَAngel keepers inscribe what you do\nبِغَائِبِينَThey will never come out of Hellfire\nلِلمُطَفِّفِينَDefrauders who give less in measure or weight"],[588,"§Al-Mutaffifin\ndeeds\nSay, \". I ask You for the delight of gazing upon Your Noble Face, and the joy of meeting You, without any harm and misleading trials befalling me.\"\nProvide water to a Muslim in charity.\nLook for someone who comes early to the mosque, and compete with him in that.\nguid\nOne of the worst punishments is being deprived of looking at the Lord, the Almighty, in the Hereafter.\nSins are the cause of stain on the heart.\nAmong the traits of the believers is competing with each other in doing righteous deeds.\nrefl\nكَلَّاۖ بَلۡۜ رَانَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِم مَّا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ١٤\nThis is the effect of one sin after another. Mujahid said: When a person sins, the sin encircles his heart, then he sins again, and the second sin encircles his heart until the sins cover his heart. Bakr bin Abdulla said: When a servant sins, his heart will have a hole as if it were pierced by a needle, then when he sins again, the same thing will repeat until his heart becomes like a sifter or screen that does not hold goodness or keep righteousness. Al-Qurtubi: 22/143.\nWhat is the stain of the heart? How does it reach the heart?\nكَلَّاۖ بَلۡۜ رَانَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِم مَّا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ١٤\nAbu Hurairah narrated that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"Verily, when the servant sins, a black spot appears on his heart. If he seeks forgiveness and repents, his heart is polished clean. But if he returns, it increases until it covers his entire heart. And that is the stain (Ran) which Allah mentions: (No! Rather, their hearts have been stained by what they used to commit).\" Al-Tabari: 24/286.\nDescribe the effect of repentance on the stain of the heart.\nكَلَّآ إِنَّهُمۡ عَن رَّبِّهِمۡ يَوۡمَئِذٖ لَّمَحۡجُوبُونَ ١٥\nAl-Husain bin Al-Fadhl said: As He barred them from His Oneness in worldly life, He will bar them from seeing Him in the Hereafter. Al-Zajjaj said: This verse proves that Allah, the Almighty, will be seen in the Hereafter. Al-Shawkani: 5/400.\nWhy will the disbelievers be barred from seeing Allah in the Hereafter?\nخِتَٰمُهُۥ مِسۡكٞۚ وَفِي ذَٰلِكَ فَلۡيَتَنَافَسِ ٱلۡمُتَنَٰفِسُونَ ٢٦\n(The competitors), those who want to hasten to the obedience of Allah. Competition is racing against others for a valuable thing and striving against oneself to emulate and draw alongside the righteous, without causing harm to others. This reflects self honor and high aspiration. Al-Alusi: 15/283.\nWhat are the good and bad competitions mentioned in this verse?\nخِتَٰمُهُۥ مِسۡكٞۚ وَفِي ذَٰلِكَ فَلۡيَتَنَافَسِ ٱلۡمُتَنَٰفِسُونَ ٢٦\nThis verse contrasts with the opening of the Surah. The defrauders strive to gather wealth through defrauding, and they will be miserable on the Day of Resurrection while the righteous will be in Bliss, and this is what they will drink, then, this is what the real competition should be for, not in defrauding in measure and weight. Al-Shanqiti: 8/463.\nWhat is the good competition and the bad one that are mentioned in this Surah?\nوَمِزَاجُهُۥ مِن تَسۡنِيمٍ ٢٧ عَيۡنٗا يَشۡرَبُ بِهَا ٱلۡمُقَرَّبُونَ ٢٨\nTasneem is the top drink in Paradise. Allah states that the drink for the righteous will be mixed with Tasneem while those who are near to Him will drink directly from Tasneem without mixing. This is because the reward fits the deed. The good deeds of those who are near to Allah are purely devoted to Him, hence, their drink will be pure. The righteous mixed their good deeds with permissible ones, and therefore, their drink will be mixed for them. Whoever kept his deeds purely to Allah, his drink will be pure, and whoever mixed his deeds, his drink will be mixed. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/270.\nThe drink of those who are near to Allah is pure, but the drink of the righteous is mixed. Why?\nوَإِذَا ٱنقَلَبُوٓاْ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِمُ ٱنقَلَبُواْ فَكِهِينَ ٣١\nMeaning: Happy and rejoicing. This was one of the greatest signs of their delusion, that they combined the worst of deeds with a sense of being secure in this world, to the extent that it was as if they had received a covenant and promise from Allah that they would be among the blessed, and they regarded themselves as being guided and the believers as being misguided. This was a fabrication against Allah, for they dared to speak about Him without knowledge. Al-Saadi: 916.\nExplain the polytheists' worst offence mentioned in this verse.\nwords\nسِجِّينٍConfinement\nمَرقُومٌClearly inscribed\nأَسَاطِيرُFables\nرَانَCovered\nالأَرَائِكِAdorned couches\nرَحِيقٍPure wine\nوَمِزَاجُهُIts mixture\nتَسنِيمٍThe highest spring in Paradise\nيَشرَبُ بِهَاThey will drink from it with joy"]])